# Presentation SPA

- Functional React + TypeScript. Slide content is components; reveal.js owns navigation.
- Wrap the deck in one component. Call `Reveal.initialize()` once after the slide DOM exists. `destroy()` on unmount or lecture change. Do not init in render or module scope.
- Horizontal `<section>` = main slides. Nested `<section>` = vertical stack. Use reveal `fragment` for stepped reveal.
- One lecture = one module that renders its `<section>` tree. Keep the wrapper generic.
- Prefer reveal.js behavior over custom keyboard/swipe code.
- Multiplex: default role on Pages is client (`secret: null`). Master runs locally with a token from `https://multiplex.up.railway.app/token`. Never commit the master secret. See `memory-bank/multiplex.md`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — re-inits every render
useEffect(() => {
  Reveal.initialize();
});

// ✅ GOOD — init once for this deck
useEffect(() => {
  const deck = new Reveal(ref.current!, options);
  deck.initialize();
  return () => {
    deck.destroy();
  };
}, [lectureId]);
```
